Undockerize + Options Parsing Refactor Plan

Goals
- [x] Fix and unify option parsing across all commands so both short flags (-c) and long flags (--cn and --cn=value) always work consistently.
- [x] Undockerize defaults: make Simple CA runnable without Docker by defaulting to XDG paths (e.g., ~/.local/state/simple-ca) while preserving Docker support via env vars.

Conventions to implement
- [x] Parsing: Use portable manual while/case argument parsing (POSIX-compatible) per repo rules; support:
  - Short flags: -f -k value -r value
  - Long flags: --force, --key-type value, --key-type=value
  - Stop parsing on --
  - -h/--help prints usage to stdout and exits 0; errors print to stderr and exit non-zero
  - Consistent error messages: "Unknown option: --xyz" and "Missing argument for --key-type"
- [x] XDG paths:
  - basePath default: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/simple-ca
  - exportDir default: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/simple-ca/export
  - rootConfig, intermediateConfig default to ${SCRIPT_DIR}/openssl-*.cnf
  - Still honor env overrides if provided (basePath, exportDir, rootConfig, intermediateConfig)
  - Add global CLI options to override paths: --base-path, --export-dir
- [ ] Maintain Docker compatibility by setting ENV in Dockerfile so container keeps /opt paths by default.

Task 1 — Normalize option parsing across all subcommands
- [x] Files:
  - [x] src/init.sh
  - [x] src/request-server-cert.sh
  - [x] src/validate.sh
  - [x] src/cert-manager.sh (already close; align behavior and messages)
- [x] Edits:
  - [x] Replace getopts-only flows with a manual while [[ $# -gt 0 ]] parser supporting both short and long options (with and without =).
  - [x] Ensure both "--opt value" and "--opt=value" are accepted for options requiring a value.
  - [x] Ensure -h|--help handled uniformly and exits 0 after printing usage.
  - [x] Standardize error messages and exit codes (2 for usage errors).
  - [x] Keep positional arguments behavior intact (e.g., re-init [archive], issue [hostname]).
- [x] Acceptance criteria:
  - [x] For each script, the following invocations behave identically:
    - short: -c value, -o value, -p value
    - long with equals: --cn=value, --output=file.tar.gz, --pass-file=path
    - long with space: --cn value, --output file.tar.gz, --pass-file path
  - [x] Unknown options error with clear message and non-zero exit.
  - [x] Missing value errors are detected for all value-taking options.

